to get to a conclusion now way.

00:11:17.319 --> 00:11:18.860
So we have something
called Meet Bot,

00:11:18.860 --> 00:11:21.502
and it's going to
help schedule a call,

00:11:21.502 --> 00:11:23.210
find the right time
between everybody who

00:11:23.210 --> 00:11:26.307
participates in this chat,
and put it on your calendar.

00:11:26.307 --> 00:11:27.890
So you don't even
have to think and go

00:11:27.890 --> 00:11:30.090
back between the
tools event schedule

00:11:30.090 --> 00:11:33.820
and what's the
people's availability.

00:11:33.820 --> 00:11:36.110
In terms of engagement
during a meeting,

00:11:36.110 --> 00:11:38.630
if you used Meet before,
you had only one layout.

00:11:38.630 --> 00:11:41.194
You could see the speaker, or
you could see the presentation.

00:11:41.194 --> 00:11:42.860
That's something that
is going to change

00:11:42.860 --> 00:11:45.500
beginning of next year,
where we are introducing

00:11:45.500 --> 00:11:46.940
adaptive layouts.

00:11:46.940 --> 00:11:50.370
The whole idea is that we know
what kind of meeting that is.

00:11:50.370 --> 00:11:52.380
Is somebody presenting,
and who is presenting?

00:11:52.380 --> 00:11:55.370
So we should show the
presentation and the speaker.

00:11:55.370 --> 00:11:57.260
Is there a presentation
and multiple people

00:11:57.260 --> 00:11:58.250
having a conversation?

00:11:58.250 --> 00:12:01.490
Then we're going to show both
the deck and the people who

00:12:01.490 --> 00:12:02.510
are talking.

00:12:02.510 --> 00:12:05.400
If it's a bunch of you
in a room just sharing

00:12:05.400 --> 00:12:07.990
a presentation of the screen,
we won't show any presenters

00:12:07.990 --> 00:12:08.490
at all.

00:12:08.490 --> 00:12:11.570
It's going to be just one
huge focus on a presentation.

00:12:11.570 --> 00:12:15.650
So basically, we are using some
basic machine learning models

00:12:15.650 --> 00:12:19.375
to make meetings more
effective and engaging.

00:12:19.375 --> 00:12:20.750
In terms of
assistance, if you're

00:12:20.750 --> 00:12:23.570
looking to use a
lot of our machine

00:12:23.570 --> 00:12:25.070
learning and voice
commands that you

00:12:25.070 --> 00:12:27.920
know with Assistant, but also
in the enterprise as well.

00:12:27.920 --> 00:12:30.920
So for customers with
Hangouts need hardware,

00:12:30.920 --> 00:12:32.420
we're introducing voice actions.

00:12:32.420 --> 00:12:34.040
So, hey, Google,
start a meeting.

00:12:34.040 --> 00:12:35.360
Or hey, Google, take notes.

00:12:35.360 --> 00:12:38.240
Or hey, Google, book this
room for under 30 minutes

00:12:38.240 --> 00:12:39.620
if it's free.

00:12:39.620 --> 00:12:41.970
The second thing is
integration with Docs.

00:12:41.970 --> 00:12:46.490
This transforms Docs from a
powerful document-editing tool

00:12:46.490 --> 00:12:48.770
into the best meeting
note-taking tool.

00:12:48.770 --> 00:12:52.400
So that's how you can track
your agenda, your action items,

00:12:52.400 --> 00:12:54.140
and take notes.

00:12:54.140 --> 00:12:55.790
This helps meeting
more productive

00:12:55.790 --> 00:12:59.540
and get everybody start
the next meeting faster

00:12:59.540 --> 00:13:01.787
and more efficient.

00:13:01.787 --> 00:13:03.620
When it comes to
brainstorming, you probably

00:13:03.620 --> 00:13:06.140
heard about Jamboard, which
is our award-winning digital

00:13:06.140 --> 00:13:07.130
whiteboard.

00:13:07.130 --> 00:13:10.850
It enables remote
teams to collaborate

00:13:10.850 --> 00:13:12.290
on an unstructured content.

00:13:12.290 --> 00:13:17.060
So drawing, getting an images,
really trying to be creative,

00:13:17.060 --> 00:13:19.070
and really getting
to coming together

00:13:19.070 --> 00:13:21.910
to bring new ideas
without having to travel,

00:13:21.910 --> 00:13:24.050
and without having
to be in person.

00:13:24.050 --> 00:13:26.690
Jamboard is completely connected
to your G Suite domain.

00:13:26.690 --> 00:13:27.582
You can share.

00:13:27.582 --> 00:13:28.290
You can continue.

00:13:28.290 --> 00:13:29.510
You can send them.

00:13:29.510 --> 00:13:31.760
You can actually explore
them and continue

00:13:31.760 --> 00:13:33.240
on where you left off.

00:13:33.240 --> 00:13:37.485
We also have mobile and tablet
applications for Jamboard,

00:13:37.485 --> 00:13:39.860
so you're not limited to just
the actual physical device.

00:13:42.384 --> 00:13:44.550
And all of these solutions
are built for enterprise.

00:13:44.550 --> 00:13:46.466
I think it's very important
to emphasize that.

00:13:46.466 --> 00:13:50.060
Even with the livestream
larger meetings, with Jamboard,

00:13:50.060 --> 00:13:53.160
it completely adheres to
the Google G Suite SLA.

00:13:53.160 --> 00:13:55.760
So two-factor authentication.

00:13:55.760 --> 00:13:58.500
We control third party access
to meetings pretty strictly.

00:13:58.500 --> 00:14:02.065
And if you do not invite third
party people to your meetings,

00:14:02.065 --> 00:14:03.690
they're not going to
be able to access.

00:14:03.690 --> 00:14:05.273
Or if you do not
allow access, they're

00:14:05.273 --> 00:14:07.230
not going to be able
to be part of it.

00:14:07.230 --> 00:14:10.320
Completely certified
for HIPAA, GDPR, ISO,

00:14:10.320 --> 00:14:16.740
SOC, and other standards that
you would expect them to be.

00:14:16.740 --> 00:14:18.530
So to summarize a
little bit, what

00:14:18.530 --> 00:14:22.580
Tyler and I were talking about
is these tools are primarily--

00:14:22.580 --> 00:14:25.340
the biggest value is that
they transform how you work.

00:14:25.340 --> 00:14:28.670
They [INAUDIBLE] mundane
tasks from email,

00:14:28.670 --> 00:14:31.070
or reduce time to join a
meeting, or make it easier

00:14:31.070 --> 00:14:32.839
for people to collaborate.

00:14:32.839 --> 00:14:34.880
And then they are deeply
integrated into G Suite,

00:14:34.880 --> 00:14:39.560
so your business process or
day-to-day habits actually

00:14:39.560 --> 00:14:40.190
are--

00:14:40.190 --> 00:14:42.230
this becomes part of
your day-to-day habits

00:14:42.230 --> 00:14:43.910
and makes it much
more streamlined

00:14:43.910 --> 00:14:45.920
to collaborate together.

00:14:45.920 --> 00:14:46.850
Built for enterprise.

00:14:46.850 --> 00:14:48.380
The slide that I just mentioned.

00:14:48.380 --> 00:14:51.600
So security compliance
and G Suite SLA.

00:14:51.600 --> 00:14:53.720
And then, finally, these
are free to anybody

00:14:53.720 --> 00:14:54.950
who's a G Suite customer.

00:14:54.950 --> 00:14:55.965
So no additional cost.

00:14:55.965 --> 00:14:57.530
And you don't need
to have any point

00:14:57.530 --> 00:15:00.350
solutions that are going to
cover any of these use cases.

